        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a4caef6c-4d48-58ef-bf3d-3da1f114d855",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rhodesia, Northern Rhodesia, Southern Rhodesia, Zambia, Zimbabwe, Ingombe Ilede, Siavonga, Kariba Dam, Zambezi River, Lusitu River\n- People: Cecil Rhodes\n- Companies: British South Africa Company\n- Organizations: British government\n- Concepts: British imperialism, protectorates, archaeology\n\nFacts:\n- In 1895, Cecil Rhodes and the British South Africa Company founded the southern African territory of Rhodesia, and the company named it after Rhodes.\n- The territory north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the British South Africa Company.\n- From 1924, the British government administered Northern Rhodesia as a protectorate under conditions similar to other British-administered protectorates, ending the special provisions used under British South Africa Company rule.\n- Northern Rhodesia has been Zambia since 1964.\n- The territory south of the Zambezi was dubbed Southern Rhodesia by the British South Africa Company.\n- Southern Rhodesia became Zimbabwe in 1980.\n- Ingombe Ilede is an archaeological site in Zambia on a hill near the confluence of the Zambezi and Lusitu rivers, near Siavonga and close to Kariba Dam.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "1c674faf-8ab0-5467-9cb7-4520114caac8",
        "text": "Page: Rhodesia (region). Sentence: The territory to the north of the Zambezi was officially designated Northern Rhodesia by the Company, and has been Zambia since 1964; that to the south, which the Company dubbed Southern Rhodesia, became Zimbabwe in 1980.\nPage: Northern Rhodesia. Sentence: From 1924 it was administered by the British government as a protectorate under similar conditions to other British-administered protectorates, and the special provisions required when it was administered by BSAC were terminated.\nPage: Cecil Rhodes. Sentence: An ardent believer in British imperialism, Rhodes and his British South Africa Company founded the southern African territory of Rhodesia (now Zimbabwe and Zambia), which the company named after him in 1895.\nPage: Ingombe Ilede. Sentence: Ingombe Ilede is an archaeological site in Zambia, on a hill near the confluence of the Zambezi and Lusitu rivers, near the town of Siavonga close to the Kariba Dam.",
